Instruction: Read the segment of a merger agreement and answer the multiple-choice question by choosing the option that best characterizes the agreement.\nQuestion: How accurate must the fundamental representations and warranties be according to the bring down provision?\nOption A: Accurate at another materiality standard (e.g., hybrid standard)\nOption B: Accurate in all material respects\nOption C: Accurate in all respects\n\nMerger Agreement: Section 5.3 Conditions to Obligations of Acquirer and Merger Sub. The obligations of Acquirer and Merger Sub to consummate the Merger are subject to the satisfaction or waiver, at or prior to the Closing, of the following conditions: (a) Representations and Warranties. The representations and warranties of the Company, except as set forth in Section 5.3(b), shall be true and correct in all respects as of the date of this Agreement and as of the Closing Date, except for inaccuracies that do not have a Material Adverse Effect. However, the fundamental representations in Sections 3.1, 3.2, and 3.3 shall be true and correct in all material respects, disregarding any materiality or Material Adverse Effect qualifications, as of the date of this Agreement and as of the Closing Date. (Page 102)
